# Suggested section for ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md

## Second opinions: dubber ruck

A local second-opinion tool is installed: `dubber-ruck` (CLI) and the `dubber-ruck`
skill. It asks a model I host myself; nothing leaves my network. It is right most of
the time but not always, so its findings are hypotheses to verify, never facts to relay.

Consult it **without being asked** at these checkpoints, by invoking the `dubber-ruck`
skill and following it:

1. After drafting a plan or design that touches three or more files or makes a
   design choice, before presenting it (`dubber-ruck plan <file>`). Leaving plan mode
   triggers this automatically through a hook; a plan drafted in conversation does not,
   so run it yourself.
2. Before committing a diff that is more than a few lines (a hook runs a quick review
   on `git commit`; if it did, use its output rather than running again).
3. When the same bug has survived two attempted fixes (`dubber-ruck duck "..."`).
4. Before anything destructive or hard to reverse.

And on demand whenever I say "duck", "second opinion", "sanity check", or "what am I
missing". Skip it for trivial edits and when I need an answer in the next minute.
Attribute its findings by name, verify before acting, and never let it override my
instructions.
